---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "APR and Fees: Origination vs Closing Costs";
const description =
  "Learn how origination fees and closing costs affect APR and total loan cost. Educational use only.";

const lastUpdated = "2026-06-25";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/guides/apr-and-fees-origination-vs-closing" lastUpdated={lastUpdated} robots="noindex, follow">
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">APR and fees</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>APR and fees: origination vs closing costs</h1>
    <p>
      APR includes certain fees but not all closing costs. This guide shows how to separate fees so your comparison stays
      accurate.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/apr-calculator">APR calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/apr-with-origination-fee">APR with origination fee</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/apr">APR topic</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Use this support page when...</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      Use this support page when the remaining question is separating lender fees from broader closing costs.
    </p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">
      If you need the stronger fee-structure guide, go back to APR with origination fee first.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">APR comparison inputs to verify</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Loan amount and term (keep them constant across offers).</li>
      <li>Nominal rate vs APR and which fees are included.</li>
      <li>Upfront fees paid in cash vs financed.</li>
      <li>Expected time horizon before refinance or payoff.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Fees that typically affect APR</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Origination fees and points.</li>
      <li>Certain lender fees required to get the loan.</li>
      <li>Some prepaid finance charges.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Costs that may not be in APR</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Appraisal, title, and recording fees.</li>
      <li>Insurance premiums and escrow setup.</li>
      <li>Taxes and transfer fees.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">How to compare offers</h2>
    <ol class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Use APR to compare finance charges.</li>
      <li>List non-APR closing costs separately.</li>
      <li>Compare total dollars paid over your time horizon.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Where to find each fee</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Loan Estimate page 1: cash to close summary.</li>
      <li>Loan Estimate page 2: itemized lender and third-party fees.</li>
      <li>Points and origination fees in the lender services section.</li>
      <li>Prepaids and escrow setup listed separately from APR fees.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Decision checklist</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Compare APR and total cost over the same horizon.</li>
      <li>Separate prepaid items from lender fees.</li>
      <li>Confirm cash-to-close for each offer.</li>
      <li>Re-run if term length or fees change.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Scenario notes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Compare a short horizon if refinancing is likely.</li>
      <li>Use the same rate and term across offers.</li>
      <li>Track lender credits separately from APR fees.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Common mistakes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Assuming APR includes every closing cost.</li>
      <li>Comparing APR without matching the loan term.</li>
      <li>Ignoring upfront cash requirements.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related tools</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/calculators/apr-calculator">APR calculator</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related guides</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/guides/apr-when-fees-are-financed">APR when fees are financed</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/discount-points-vs-lender-credits">Points vs credits</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">FAQ</h2>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Can two loans have the same APR but different cash to close?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      Yes. APR focuses on finance charges, while cash to close includes many other costs.
    </p>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Should I compare APR or total cost?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      Use both. APR is a good comparison, but total dollars paid over your horizon is the final decision metric.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/apr-calculator">Compare APR offers</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/apr-when-fees-are-financed">APR when fees are financed</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/apr">APR topic</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-06-25</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>





